Description: Implements exponential factor models for dimensionality reduction 
    and factor analysis of non-Gaussian data. Extends traditional factor analysis 
    to handle count data, binary data, and other exponential family distributions 
    using efficient optimization algorithms including Laplacian approximation, 
    simulated maximum likelihood, and posterior sampling methods.
